{
  "name": "CE-00 | Error Handler",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## CE-00 | Error Handler\n**What it does:** any workflow that names this one as its *Error Workflow* calls it when an execution fails.\n\n**Steps**\n1. **Error Trigger** receives the failed workflow's name, the node that broke, the error message and a link to the execution.\n2. A row is added to the **Errors** tab of your Google Sheet.\n3. An email is sent to `notifyEmail` (set in the *Config* node).\n\n**Setup:** open each of the other 5 workflows -> Settings (three dots) -> *Error workflow* -> choose this one.\n\n**Good to know:** error workflows only fire for *automatic* runs (schedules), not when you click *Execute workflow* manually.\nRows that fail mid-way keep a status in the sheet (e.g. `Generating`, `Rendering`). Set them back to the previous status to retry.",
        "height": 330,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "c4edf4ee-c5ce-5ed8-841c-b59b19d6d89b",
      "name": "Note - How this works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -80,
        -60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "9a1dc297-7465-5b97-9ebd-e9e8b8ff13c4",
      "name": "Error Trigger",
